chris@chrism.demon.co.uk (Chris Marriott) writes:
>I've just spent all evening playing Nethack on the PC (v3.1.1), regularly
>saving the game "just in case".  I then got killed, and found that my
>character is permanently gone - no way to restart from the last savegame!!!

>Is this REALLY the way it works - it just seems - well - permanent :-)
>Do you really have to start the whole thing again each time you die?

Death is permanent, unless you're playing in wizard mode.  (And then it won't
score your game.)  A lot of newcomers to Nethack are used to other games where
restoring savefiles is routine, and they are in for a very rude surprise.
Nethack is designed to be won _without_ the use of savefiles, and there are
safeguards written into the code to insure that this occurs.  Nethack is also
very difficult to win.  I have won only a half dozen times or so, and I've been
playing the various versions for four years now...

The bottom line is:  When you die, that's it.  Your character is gone for good.
Deal with it, and start your next character.  You are also going to discover
that Nethack is _not_ a forgiving game.  One misstep, one single mistake can
be an error your character will not live long enough to regret.

